{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root-cause measurement and real-data result (2026-11-18 PST, rebar-session-3d705fec). Fix is on branch veery-verify-identity-perf, commit 6149d61c008 (not yet pushed; make verify running).\n\n**Before the fix, original history** (fresh no-remote TMPDIR clone of origin/tickets b878d77e28d, 310,079 commits, GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES set): enforced `verify-identity --all` profiled for 16 min classified 7,553 of 50,493 events (~90 ms/event, projecting ~75 min plus maps). Per-event cost: 13,266 `git merge-base` (456 s, ~34 ms each), 6,780 `ssh -V` (90 s) + 6,780 `ssh-keygen -Y verify` (104 s); two identical ~110 s full-history `git log` walks for the two maps. 0 per-position fallbacks on this history (1 of 44,311 ledger positions misses the `*.json` map).\n**Reclaimed history** (previous dry-run shadow, 13,196 commits): 37,917 of 44,238 ledger positions and 2 identity keyring positions miss the `*.json` map → one full-history walk each, the keyring ones per event. Including `*.json.retired` adds resolves all; 37,916 of 37,917 resolve to the commit the reclaim already stored (the other had a null stored commit_sha).\n\n**After the fix, merged dry-run harness** (`python -m rebar._commands.reclaim_dry_run --source <fresh clone> --ref refs/heads/tickets --horizon-days 30`, workdir $TMPDIR/veery-3d705fec/dryrun, exit 0, ok=true): T0 b878d77e28d -> new tip fb999892b1e on the file:// fake remote; commits 310,079 -> 12,675; blobless pack 639,953 KiB -> 101,712 KiB (99.3 MiB); reduced state equal; enforce_since on branch; source ref unchanged.\n- ENFORCED `verify-identity --all`, original history: **27 min 1 s (1,621 s), FAIL (exit 1)** — 42,612 verified, 874 unsigned, 0 unknown-author, 7,007 bad-signature, 0 key-not-valid-at-era (50,493 in scope).\n- ENFORCED `verify-identity --all`, rewritten history: **20 min 40 s (1,240 s), FAIL (exit 1)** — identical counts.\n(Host was also running make verify; a standalone fixed run on the original clone took 26 min 7 s with the same verdict.)\n\nVerdict: the reclaim changes no verdict, so this is not a reclaim defect. The enforced check fails on BOTH histories because of 7,007 SNAPSHOT-ledger entries (all ledger, none live) classified bad-signature: ~4,987 are signed by two keys never recorded on identity 594c's keyring, ~1,320 by keyring keys but recorded `signer_pubkey: null` at compaction. Filed as starving-sphalerite-skua (df01-290f), discovered_from this ticket, relates_to the epic. No live tickets store or origin/tickets was pushed, reset or force-updated."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795035466022770102,"uuid":"b08334e3-fab3-4ea1-8b09-4017efba647b"}